<title>USA: Conn. $79.8 mln deal priced at 5.30 pct top yield.</title>
<headline>Conn. $79.8 mln deal priced at 5.30 pct top yield.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>JP Morgan Securities Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $79.8 million Connecticut refunding bonds at a top yield of 5.30 percent in 2009.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>STATE OF CONNECTICUT</p>
<p>RE: $79,760,000*</p>
<p>SPECIAL TAX OBLIGATION REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>TRANSPORTATION INFRASTRUCTURE PURPOSES</p>
<p>1996 SERIES C</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>  MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA		   FITCH: AAA</p>
<p>	     (A1)			 (AA-)		 (AA-)</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>  DATED: 10/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
